{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"5db5287a-27c1-431f-8376-9d67e3908e01","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"deepseek-flash","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"No android/ directory — product code not delivered. I must write JUnit4 Kotlin tests that output \"待测：模块未交付\" when product not delivered, and they need to be structured to compile in CI once product exists but currently... Hmm, tricky. The tests refer to product classes that don't exist. If the classes don't exist, the test won't compile. The requirement: \"产品代码未交付时：测试必须清楚输出“待测：模块未交付”并以 pytest skip（或脚本退出码 0 + 该提示）结束，不能伪装通过。\"\n\nFor Android JVM tests, the equivalent is to detect at runtime? But compilation fails if product classes absent. Options:\n1. Write the tests with class names defined as constants at top, and use reflection to load classes at runtime, so tests compile even when product classes absent. Then use `Assume.assumeTrue` (JUnit4) to skip with message \"待测：模块未交付\". That's the cleanest approach: reflection avoids compile-time dependency on product classes entirely. That fits \"不要编造产品的函数名：需要产品入口时，在脚本顶部集中定义成常量/待定项，并注释'待写手交付后对齐'\".\n\nBut `./gradlew testDebugUnitTest` requires an Android project. The task says only create files under `tests/android/android-diagnostics/`. Not the android/ product dir. So how would gradle run? Probably the test files are placed in the android project later (the writer's project), or there is a standalone gradle harness under tests/android/android-diagnostics. Task: \"写 JUnit4 Kotlin 测试草稿（按仓库根相对路径读向量；类名来自 brief，包名待对齐放顶部）... 脚本面向 GitHub Actions，本机不装 JDK/SDK/.NET、不跑构建；脚本顶部标注'待 CI'。... 运行环境 ubuntu-latest，./gradlew testDebugUnitTest。\"\n\nHmm, \"只准改：tests/android/android-diagnostics/ 下的文件\". So we can create a standalone Gradle project there? But no new dependencies except JUnit. A JVM Kotlin project under tests/android/android-diagnostics would need Kotlin plugin & JUnit. But \"脚本\" suggests maybe a shell script wrapper that runs in CI. Let me check other test cards / tests/INDEX.md and existing patterns (tests/server is pytest). Let me look at tests/INDEX.md and scripts, and the previous android-diagnostics cli log perhaps describes environment.\n\nAlso, the test files are drafts intended to be run by CI. Given no JDK locally, we should create:\n- `tests/android/android-diagnostics/run.sh` script (CI entrypoint) that checks for product code and runs gradle? But we can't modify android/ build files. Hmm.\n\nLet me re-read: \"写 JUnit4 Kotlin 测试草稿（按仓库根相对路径读向量；类名来自 brief，包名待对齐放顶部），不新增 JUnit 以外依赖。脚本面向 GitHub Actions，本机不装 JDK/SDK/.NET、不跑构建；脚本顶部标注'待 CI'。产品代码未交付时输出'待测：模块未交付'。运行环境 ubuntu-latest，./gradlew testDebugUnitTest。\"\n\nSo the deliverable is Kotlin test file(s) under tests/android/android-diagnostics/, plus maybe a run.sh. The `./gradlew testDebugUnitTest` indicates it'll be run in the android project once delivered. Perhaps the tests are placed under tests/ but CI copies them into android/app/src/test? That's CI's (ci-guards) job. Our job: write the test sources + a script that CI can invoke, that copies/links? But scope says only tests/android/android-diagnostics/.\n\nSimplest complete approach:\n1. `tests/android/android-diagnostics/` contains Kotlin JUnit4 test files:\n   - `LogRedactorTest.kt` (or one combined `DiagnosticsTest.kt`?) — task lists three test areas: redaction, invite code, admin-contract parse validation. Brief says classes LogRedactor, InviteCode, and an admin-contract parse/validate function. Separate test classes are natural.\n2. Since product code isn't delivered, tests must skip gracefully. But Kotlin compile-time references fail. Use reflection + `Assume.assumeTrue`/`assumeFalse`. But also if classes absent, `Assume` will mark tests skipped — but message displays? `Assume.assumeTrue(\"待测：模块未交付\", available)`. Yes.\n3. HOWEVER: test file reading vector JSON needs JSON parsing. No dependencies besides JUnit. Android instrumentation has org.json, but JVM unit tests: Android's org.json is stubbed in unit tests (throws \"not mocked\") unless using Robolectric or Gradle unit test options returning default values. So cannot use org.json in local JVM unit tests. We need to parse JSON without deps. Options: `kotlinx.serialization` (new dep, not allowed), or write a tiny hand parser (ugly, ~150 lines), or use regex/manual extraction tailored to the known vector shapes. Hmm.\n\nWait — product uses org.json manually for admin-contract parsing (\"为 0.2.0 预留的响应校验用 org.json 手写\"). For unit tests, if Android Gradle plugin `testOptions.unitTests.isReturnDefaultValues` or the project uses `org.json:json` test dependency... but we cannot add dependencies. Task says \"不新增 JUnit 以外依赖\". So test code must not depend on org.json.\n\nCould read vector JSON and parse with a minimal parser. The test vectors are small and stable; a tiny JSON parser (~100 lines) in Kotlin is acceptable, but ponytail says minimum code. Alternatively, use `javax.script` (Nashorn gone in JDK 15+) — no.\n\nCould parse with regex per vector shape. redaction.json: extract pairs \"in\" and \"out\". invite-code: valid/invalid arrays, need to distinguish JSON null (invalid case includes null). admin-contract: nested structures — regex parsing is fragile.\n\nA minimal hand-written JSON parser handling objects/arrays/strings/numbers/booleans/null is ~80–120 lines. That's the correct-on-edge-cases choice. Since it's test infrastructure, and ponytail allows \"whole new script or app leaves one small test or self-check\". We can include a self-check test? Maybe not needed.\n\nAlternatively, JSON parsing could be avoided by using the JSON files as strings and a small helper. Let me think about actual requirement: \"按仓库根相对路径读向量\". So test reads `shared/test-vectors/redaction.json` etc. Resolve repo root: walk up from user.dir until `shared/test-vectors` exists. Good.\n\nNow reflection for product classes. Brief says classes: `LogRedactor`, `InviteCode` (isValid), and admin-contract parse validation function. Package name TBD at top as constant. Since we can't guess function names, we use constants:\n- `LOG_REDACTOR_CLASS` = \"com.osakaconnect.diagnostics.LogRedactor\" (待写手交付后对齐)\n- `REDACT_METHOD` = \"redact\" (待写手交付后对齐)\n- `INVITE_CODE_CLASS` = \"...InviteCode\"; `IS_VALID_METHOD` = \"isValid\"\n- Admin contract: class/method TBD. The function per brief is \"admin-contract 解析校验函数\". Name unknown. We define constants `ADMIN_CONTRACT_CLASS` / `PARSE_METHOD` and test valid/invalid using reflection. But signature unknown: does it throw on invalid, return null, or return boolean? We can define expectation: \"解析校验函数\" — likely `parse(json: String): T?` or throws. Since unknown, we need to define contract at top as assumptions. The task card says \"admin-contract.json 解析校验函数正反例\" — test it. Since function unknown, we could define the contract we test: a function `validate(rawJson: String, schemaName: String): Boolean`? But that's inventing. Better: define a top-level \"待定项\" with a documented assumption: call `ADMIN_CONTRACT_CLASS.ADMIN_CONTRACT_METHOD` with raw JSON; invalid → returns null or throws; valid → non-null. Hmm, inventing semantics.\n\nLet me check the previous android-diagnostics CLI log — it may contain session context/requirements, and maybe other branches contain android code. Let me also check notes/win-diagnostics.md for parallel naming (Windows side) and memory. The log may reveal what was already attempted.\n\nLet me read the cli log and win-diagnostics brief.","signature":"5db5287a-27c1-431f-8376-9d67e3908e01"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1339,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":17280,"output_tokens":0,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c5b32248-d525-4117-8e3f-453c96726101","uuid":"e2a64a88-81da-412a-8a24-fcaf1e60b4d7","timestamp":"2026-11-02T05:02:25.136Z","thinking_duration_ms":11742,"thinking_display":"updates"}
