need a defined contract. Options at top:\n```kotlin\n// 产品入口（写手交付后对齐）：\nconst val ADMIN_CONTRACT_CLASS = \"com.osakaconnect.diagnostics.AdminContract\"\nconst val ADMIN_CONTRACT_METHOD = \"parseAndValidate\" // signature: (String, String) -> Any?\n```\nBut if name/signature differ, test will fail/skip? If class exists but method missing, reflection throws NoSuchMethodException → test fails. That's correct-ish: signals misalignment, but could be a false failure. The task explicitly says don't invent function names; define as constants with \"待写手交付后对齐\". But then how to write a meaningful test? We define the expected contract at top and note it must be aligned. Maybe better: the admin parse function is described in brief as \"admin-contract 解析校验函数\" with no name. We can define:\n- Class: `AdminContractValidator`\n- Method: `validate(rawJson: String, schema: String): Boolean`? Hmm.\n\nMaybe more robust: define a small set of candidate method names/signatures and adapt? That's over-engineering. The task expects a draft with constants to align. I'll define the contract clearly:\n```kotlin\n// 待写手交付后对齐：类/方法名与返回约定。\n// 约定：first arg = schema 名（HealthResponse/VersionResponse/ErrorBody），second = JSON 文本；\n// 合法返回非 null/true；非法返回 null/false 或抛异常，均视为拒收。\n```\nAnd test both acceptance semantics: valid must not reject; invalid must be rejected. Implement helper that tries boolean or non-null or no-throw. But if a method doesn't exist → assume skip \"待测：接口未对齐\"? Hmm, product delivered but mismatched should fail rather than skip to avoid false pass. Yet the task says \"不要编造产品的函数名：需要产品入口时，在脚本顶部集中定义成常量/待定项\". So define constants; if they don't match, test fails with clear message. That's acceptable and honest. But maybe use `Assume` only when whole module absent (android dir missing / class missing), and fail if class present but method missing. Reasonable.\n\nHowever run.sh early-exits if android/ absent, so test files won't run now anyway. The reflection+assume is for the case where android/ exists (android-shell branch) but diagnostics module not yet delivered. In that case classes absent → skip. Good.\n\nClass/method:\n- LogRedactor: likely object/class with `redact(String): String`. Windows brief says LogRedactor. Android shell summary says \"生命周期回调经 LogRedactor 记录\". Package likely `com.osakaconnect.diagnostics.LogRedactor` or `com.osakaconnect.shell.LogRedactor`? Could be `com.osakaconnect.shell`. Since android-shell uses package `com.osakaconnect.shell` and diagnostics is a separate module branch also likely same app package. The brief doesn't state package. We define candidates? \"包名待对齐放顶部\" — so put ONE package constant at top and note alignment. I'll choose `com.osakaconnect.diagnostics` as product package and test package. Hmm, but if product is in `com.osakaconnect.shell`, tests fail. Better define `PRODUCT_PACKAGE` constant used for all class lookups, separate from test's own package. Test package must match its location when copied (`com.osakaconnect.diagnostics`). Actually test package can be anything as long as file path matches source set? Kotlin doesn't enforce path, but Gradle compiles all under src/test/java regardless of package path. So test package free; class lookups use `PRODUCT_PACKAGE + \".LogRedactor\"`. Define:\n```kotlin\nprivate const val PRODUCT_PACKAGE = \"com.osakaconnect.diagnostics\" // 待写手交付后对齐\nprivate val LOG_REDACTOR_CLASS = \"$PRODUCT_PACKAGE.LogRedactor\"\nprivate const val LOG_REDACT_METHOD = \"redact\"\n...\n```\nFor InviteCode.isValid: object or companion? Could be `InviteCode.isValid(String)`. Reflection must handle object INSTANCE, companion, static, or instance constructor. A helper that finds method and invokes with an instance if needed:\n\n```kotlin\nprivate fun invokeStatic(className: String, methodName: String, vararg args: Any?): Any? {\n    val cls = Class.forName(className)\n    val m = cls.methods.firstOrNull { it.name == methodName && it.parameterCount == args.size } ?: error(\"...\")\n